thread:
maria_docs: opened PR #842 to overhaul the 429 troubleshooting section — aiming to add a short sample that shows graceful fallback when context trimming is needed. PTAL when you have a sec.

alex_sdk: saw it, thanks. can you add a tiny JS snippet that shows: detect 429 -> try prompt-abridge -> retry with same model? that helps SDK users.

sam_oncall: also include a brief note about exponential backoff + max attempts (we keep seeing retries without jitter).

lisa_prod: fwiw prod apps prefer switching to a smaller model variant first (cheaper) instead of immediate trim. maybe show both options.

maria_docs: good call. plan: add two short examples — (1) fallback-to-smaller-model, (2) prompt-abridge-and-retry. keep each <12 lines. will also add a short troubleshooting checklist at top.

alex_sdk: for the JS sample, use our unified SDK pattern: 
```js
// pseudocode, keep short
try {
  await client.responses.create({model: 'redwood-xlarge', input});
} catch (err) {
  if (err.status === 429) {
    // simplest: try smaller model
    await client.responses.create({model: 'redwood-medium', input});
  }
}
```

maria_docs: thanks — i'll adapt that and add an abridge helper snippet. any suggestions for the abridge heuristic? keep it deterministic (truncate last 20% then prefer pruning assistant messages).

sam_oncall: include guidance: prefer clipping assistant/system first, then user messages from oldest -> newest. also warn about losing critical instructions. link to evals checklist.

lisa_prod: add note: measure output quality delta after fallback; add quick telemetry example: increment metric "doc.429.fallback_used". product teams want that telemetry snippet.

docs-bot: checklist reminder: docs PRs that touch error-handling must include: 1) short code samples, 2) one human-readable runbook line, 3) link to relevant SDK helper functions, 4) unit test or sample harness.

maria_docs: added the checklist to the PR description and a small unit test that runs the abridge helper on a long conversation. @alex_sdk can you review the sample naming and API surface?

alex_sdk: will review today. quick nit: prefer function name `abridgePromptForContext` not `trimPrompt`. clearer semantics. also add an inline comment about preserving the last user message.

maria_docs: done in the branch. pushed commit, asking for one more read. hoping to merge before end of sprint. thanks all :rocket:

sam_oncall: if merged, tag release notes team — this is behavior users might rely on. we should call out the recommended fallback order.

lisa_prod: I'll draft a short blurb for the release notes after merge.

alex_sdk: LGTM from me after the naming tweak.

maria_docs: merging in ~10m unless an objection. thanks for quick turnaround. :thumbsup:

(automated) docs-bot: PR #842 status -> ready for merge (checks green)

maria_docs: merged. leaving a follow-up ticket to add a short sample that shows telemetry snippet with envoy-style counters.

alex_sdk: great, will add a cross-reference in the SDK README next sprint.
